.TH RATTSC 1 "2026-10-05" "Rattpack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rattsc \- interpret, lint, and test Rattscript
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rattsc
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B rattsc \--lint
.I FILE
.br
.B rattsc \-e
.I SCRIPT
.br
.B rattsc \--test
.I DIRECTORY
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rattsc
is the standalone tree-walking Rattscript interpreter, interactive REPL,
annotation linter, and golden-test runner. Select one mode per invocation.
With a file, the evaluator's working directory is that file's directory.
Inline evaluation and the REPL use the invoking directory. Files ending in .in
are preprocessed as Rattscript templates before running or linting.
.PP
Rattscript supports dynamic values, optional type annotations, lexical
functions, control flow, imports, and namespaced standard-library modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--lint
Check FILE and statically imported source modules without executing module
top-level statements. Template substitutions required to parse .in files
are evaluated. Linting is not a full build-spec validator or execution
simulator.
.TP
.BI \-e " SCRIPT" ", \--eval=" SCRIPT
Evaluate a source string. Quote the string to protect it from shell expansion.
.TP
.BI \--test= DIRECTORY
Recursively run .ratt golden fixtures and compare captured output byte-for-byte
with sibling .expected files. A diagnostic contributes its code to captured
output. Missing expected files, mismatches, or an empty directory fail.
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \--version
Display the version and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE USE
With no arguments, display the ratt> prompt. Bindings persist between inputs;
the last statement's value is printed unless it is nil. Use :q, :quit, or
end-of-input to exit. Unmatched opening braces cause a continuation prompt,
"... ". Brace counting also sees braces in strings; use files for complicated
multiline input. Runtime diagnostics are displayed and leave the prompt usable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, help, or version output; 1 indicates an application
diagnostic or failing golden tests; 2 indicates argument parsing failure.
Diagnostics go to standard error; script output goes to standard output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rattsc hello.ratt
rattsc \--lint tools/helpers.ratt
rattsc \-e 'fn square(x: int) -> int { return x * x } print(square(7))'
rattsc \--test tests/script
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rattbuild (1),
.BR rattpkg (1),
.BR rattspec (1),
.BR ratt-language-server (1)
.PP
The installed Rattpack manual contains the language and standard-library
reference.
